    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n422" root="ادب" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْبٌ</span></b> , (S, M, K,) or, accord. to some, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِدْبٌ</span></b> ,
(TA,) <i>Wonderful;</i> or <i>a wonderful thing;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجَبٌ</span>; (S, M, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُدْبَةٌ</span></b>  [used in the
latter sense]. (K.) You say, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ فُلَانٌ بِأَمْرٍ إِدْبٍ</span></b> 
<i>Such a one did a wonderful thing.</i> (As, T. *) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدَبٌ</span>, last sentence.

